    "content": "Mogadishu, September 12, 2026 — Prime Minister Hamsa Abdi Barre of Somalia's federal government convened a meeting with his cabinet ministers on Saturday to evaluate the performance of various ministries. The review focused on the implementation of plans and commitments previously set by the ministers, examining what has been accomplished, obstacles encountered, and areas requiring adjustment or acceleration.\n\nThe assessment is part of the government's ongoing efforts to ensure accountability and drive progress on key national priorities. Each ministry was measured against specific work plans and targets agreed upon earlier. The Prime Minister emphasized the importance of delivering on promises made to the public and urged ministers to address shortcomings promptly.\n\nThis performance review comes amid heightened expectations from Somali citizens and the international community for tangible results from the current administration. The government has faced criticism over the pace of reforms and service delivery, making such evaluations crucial for maintaining credibility and public trust.\n\nFor the Somali diaspora, these developments are significant as many diaspora members closely follow governance and development in their homeland. They often invest remittances, skills, and knowledge in Somali institutions and expect transparency and effectiveness from federal ministries. The review signals a push for better performance, which could impact diaspora engagement and confidence in government-led initiatives.\n\nThe meeting concluded with directives for ministries to enhance their efforts and meet outstanding targets. The Prime Minister's office did not release detailed outcomes per ministry, but the review is expected to inform future budget allocations and policy adjustments.\n\nRead the original report from Radio Dalsan here: https://radiodalsan.com/2026/09/12/wasiirrada-xamsa-oo-shaashad-lagu-kala-sarreysiiyay/?utm_source=rss&#038;utm_medium=rss&#038;utm_campaign=wasiirrada-xamsa-oo-shaashad-lagu-kala-sarreysiiyay",
